  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The citation is a `habeas:coverage` exception on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs` `impl[UnreadContents/NodeContents]/fn[fingerprint]`. The function body is `match *self {}`. That match has no arms, so it has no executable case.\n\nThe commentary says `UnreadContents` is uninhabited, and the source agrees: `enum[UnreadContents]` is declared as `enum UnreadContents {}`, so no value of it can exist. Nothing can call `fingerprint`, so zero execution is expected.\n\nThe commentary also says the implementation exists to satisfy the `Domain` associated-type bound. That matches `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/type[NodeContent]`, which sets `NodeContent = UnreadContents`. The `node_content` guard panics, so the fixture never reads contents.\n\nThe reason is substantive, not just difficulty. The commentary sits in fenced citation commentary on the function, as the built-in requires. It agrees with the current source. The citation is on an explicit function with a body, which the built-in allows.",
